  "findings": [
    "With only January crops completed, the season inputs are constant, so the GP cannot learn the season effect before the second wave: gp-bo-v2 started exactly the same second-wave policies as gp-bo-v1.",
    "After the July crops complete, the season-aware model separates the plantings (seed 1: 44.6 January, 25.6 July; seed 2: 48.2 and 30.1), consistent with observed July outcomes of about 12-30. The predicted scored value of the recommendation falls from 44.7/50.5 (season-blind) to 35.1/39.2.",
    "Learning the season effect earlier would require planting in another season before day 182, e.g. a staggered start; this is a genuine scheduling trade-off for agents."
  ]
